    {
      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:c3205ac1e20a266d",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "a41ca45a64f9055383539f1e5f4cb314ada20bbd7df624040a87d1d8605200f0",
      "text": "Breakfast at the hotel. \n\nToday you will go on a city tour to the most interesting sights in Santiago from the historical city to the modern buildings. We will pass through the Alameda Bernardo O´Higgins Ave, where´s Palacio Presidencial de la Moneda, then we will walk by the streets of Huerfanos and Ahumada that take us to Plaza de Armas. We will see the Cathedral, The Post Office and the Council of Santiago. After that, we´ll take a look at Santa Lucia Mountain, strategic point of the city foundation. We´ll continue through Parque Forestal and the Fine Art Museum. Crossing the Mapocho river, we will arrive to Bellavista Suburb, a bohemian place with strong cultural activity. Nearby is the entrance to Parque Metropolitano with San Cristobal Mountain from where we will be able to appreciate the whole city. We will finish our tour visiting the new city center, Providencia and Las Condes and Vitacura suburbs.Transfer to the hotel.\n\nOptional tour  with tasting to the wineries in the Maipo Valley. The price per person is  $230 (minimum 2 pax)",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "word_exact",
        "fileId": "1J3iiKe3a157uLe4QAeKgqNdlhrMV3lAa",
